Captured: 2026-07-29 (UTC), immediately after implementing
           mcp/sdd-forge-mcp/src/path-guard.ts
Host: Darwin 25.5.0 arm64; node v24.13.0; npm 11.6.2

STAGE: GREEN. Red and Green are SEPARATE files. The red state is in
specs/epic-136-phase4-mcp/verification/T-003/red.log, captured before this
src/ edit existed (its header carries the git status / git diff --stat proof
that src/ and dist/ were untouched at that moment). Green is re-confirmed
after the rebuilt dist/index.js is committed, in
specs/epic-136-phase4-mcp/verification/T-003/dist-parity.log.

What was implemented (design.md API/Contract Plan, followed literally):
  * exported interfaces GuardedListError { path, reason } and
    GuardedListResult { files, errors };
  * a private errorMessage(error: unknown): string helper -- the ONLY
    genuinely new logic;
  * exported listGuardedFilesWithDiagnostics(root, relDir), carrying the walk
    that was previously inside listGuardedFiles, with its two bare `catch {}`
    blocks converted to `catch (error) { errors.push(...) }` and its control
    flow otherwise untouched (still `return`s past a top-level readdirSync
    failure, still `continue`s past a per-entry statSync failure);
  * listGuardedFiles reduced to
      return listGuardedFilesWithDiagnostics(root, relDir).files;
    with its exported signature intact and its stale doc sentence ("callers
    that need the failure reason should use `resolveGuarded` instead") updated
    to name the new function.

GUARD ORDERING (security-spec.md B3): resolveGuardedDirectory(root, relDir) is
the FIRST statement of the new function, OUTSIDE and BEFORE both try/catch
blocks, and its failure returns { files: [], errors: [ ... ] } immediately --
no readdirSync/statSync is reached. The allowlist/denylist rules themselves
(ALLOWLISTED_DIRECTORIES / ALLOWLISTED_FILES / DENYLISTED_BASENAMES) are not
touched at all (BL-006). See selfcheck.log for the byte-identity diff of those
constants and for the mutation experiment that proves the ordering assertions
are not vacuous.

